  promptText: A foreign firm offers to buy rights to your reforested land as carbon
    credits for a large sum. Accepting delivers immediate funds but transfers control
    and decision-making away from the community; refusing keeps sovereignty but forgoes
    rapid capital.
  leftAnswer: Selling can fund urgent needs and services your people require now.
  rightAnswer: Keeping control preserves your right to steward the land for generations.
